WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.325
The migration runs as six waves.

2
00:00:02.325 --> 00:00:07.338
Each wave's exit gate is the next one's
entry gate, and each has its own rollback.

3
00:00:07.338 --> 00:00:11.931
The durations are program planning
figures for a single-forest estate,

4
00:00:11.931 --> 00:00:15.200
not commitments; scale them
to the wave 1 inventory.

5
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.125
Appendix A turns each
wave into a checklist

6
00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:20.888
with an owner and a verification per line.

7
00:00:20.888 --> 00:00:26.046
Wave 1, Assess, weeks one to four:
inventory every CA and template,

8
00:00:26.046 --> 00:00:30.511
run the Chapter 03 checklist,
classify every template,

9
00:00:30.511 --> 00:00:35.274
list every relying party, and
run the strong-mapping sweep.

10
00:00:35.274 --> 00:00:37.762
It reads, so it needs no rollback.

11
00:00:37.762 --> 00:00:42.380
Wave 2, Foundation: create the
Cloud PKI CAs with licensed keys,

12
00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.997
upload user-issuing CAs to the
Entra trust store, deploy trust

13
00:00:46.997 --> 00:00:52.338
profiles and the cloud chain to
domain-joined relying parties, and test.

14
00:00:52.338 --> 00:00:57.011
The gate is trust profiles on at
least ninety-nine percent of managed

15
00:00:57.011 --> 00:01:01.275
devices and every CRL reachable
from inside, outside and Entra.

16
00:01:01.275 --> 00:01:07.251
Wave 3, Pilot, fifty to a hundred
devices: Wi-Fi then VPN, then CBA through

17
00:01:07.251 --> 00:01:13.437
staged rollout, with AD CS autoenrollment
left on so the rollback works.

18
00:01:13.437 --> 00:01:16.675
The gate is ninety-five
percent issuance success.

19
00:01:16.675 --> 00:01:20.139
Wave 4, Scale, in rings;
remove autoenrollment for

20
00:01:20.139 --> 00:01:23.863
each ring once its cloud
certificates are accepted.

21
00:01:23.863 --> 00:01:26.744
Wave 5, Cutover: record
federation settings,

22
00:01:26.744 --> 00:01:31.626
convert domains starting with the
smallest, and keep AD FS restorable for

23
00:01:31.626 --> 00:01:36.749
thirty days, which is what makes the
four-hour recovery objective achievable.

24
00:01:36.749 --> 00:01:38.587
Wave 6, Decommission.

25
00:01:38.587 --> 00:01:43.031
The rules across waves: rehearse
each rollback in a test scope first,

26
00:01:43.031 --> 00:01:47.475
and never let a rollback depend on
a component the same wave retires.

27
00:01:47.475 --> 00:01:52.180
Removing or editing a SCEP profile
revokes its certificates on Windows

28
00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:56.710
and Apple platforms, so treat profile
changes as changes with impact.
